**Summary:**

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` instead of `parts[0]`, which caused it to return the second word instead of the first word. This resulted in:
- `test_basic` failing because `'hello world'` returned `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- `test_single` erroring because `'solo'` only has one word, so accessing index 1 caused an IndexError

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first element of the split string.
